  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper compares a variational quantum neural network (VQNN) with classical LSTM and multiple linear regression (MLR) models for predicting low stock prices of CRDB and NMB banks using 2,525 historical samples. Classical models outperform the quantum model, achieving higher predictive accuracy (e.g., R² ≈ 0.994 for MLR vs ≤0.9901 for VQNN on CRDB data) and lower MAPE, while the VQNN shows inconsistent performance across epochs. No quantum hardware, qubit counts, or computational speedups are reported.",
